{"type":"text","timestamp":1794531893497,"sessionID":"ses_e2d947514ffe5OrPhqo7f5giqK","part":{"id":"prt_1d26f8fc0002VsqXgpZIvcC8oE","sessionID":"ses_e2d947514ffe5OrPhqo7f5giqK","messageID":"msg_1d26f8501001GrBmZjuJUCxCe3","type":"text","text":"T014 is complete.\n\n## Files written\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`\n  - `runnablePolicy` became `runnablePolicyRecord`, returning the whole `commandPolicies` record so the policy and its `mutating` class come from one lookup. The strictest-route reduce now compares and returns records.\n  - `renderCommandRows` adds `mutating` to the row after `policy`, emitted only when the record states a class, so the rerendered line keeps the shape `{ command, policy, mutating, ownerSkillId }`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`\n  - Added `readonly mutating?: 'read-only' | 'add-only' | 'mutates';` to `CommandRow` outside the generated block, and the interface comment now names the class.\n  - The generated `COMMAND_ROWS` block was rewritten by the deriver, not by hand. The generated JSON did not change.\n\n## Verify output\n\n```\n$ node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -r .status\nfresh\n\n$ rg -c \"'command-doctor-git-setup': \\{ command: '/doctor:git setup', policy: 'run', mutating: 'read-only'\" .../lib/command-attach.ts\n1\n\n$ rg -c \"'command-doctor-speckit': \\{ command: '/doctor:speckit', policy: 'run', mutating: 'add-only'\" .../lib/command-attach.ts\n1\n\n$ npm run typecheck            # in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime\n> typecheck\n> ../../system-spec-kit/node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit --composite false -p tsconfig.build.json\nTYPECHECK_EXIT=0\n\n$ npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  14 passed (14)\n```\n\nAll 55 `COMMAND_ROWS` entries carry a class (`2 add-only`, `36 mutates`, `17 read-only`). `git status` for the three candidate paths shows only the two files above modified, and the generated bridge JSON is unchanged. No checkbox was ticked.\n\n## Operator action\n\nT014 stays `[ ]` for you to mark. Nothing else is outstanding.","time":{"start":1794531889088,"end":1794531893497}}}
